            <title>[LU-20979] sanity test_255a: ladvise willread fails with EIO (cannot give advice)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20979</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_255a's ladvise_willread_performance() calls lfs ladvise -a willread partway through its willread/OSS-cache/ladvise speed loop. On session a392d6e5-43e1-445b-a511-479fc5528462 (review-ldiskfs, build 133644, patch 69392 ps2) the call failed outright: lfs ladvise: cannot give advice: Input/output error (5). This is a FAIL with a concrete EIO, not the hang covered by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20976" title="sanity test_255a: willread/ladvise speed loop hangs, session TIMEOUT" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20976"&gt;LU-20976&lt;/a&gt; (session TIMEOUT, no PASS/FAIL recorded) nor the performance-mismatch defects of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16449" title="sanity test_255a defect: ladvise failed, test PASS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16449"&gt;LU-16449&lt;/a&gt; (ladvise failed, test PASS) or &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15350" title="sanity test_255a defect: ladvise: range [2, 1] is invalid" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15350"&gt;LU-15350&lt;/a&gt; (range &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;2, 1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; is invalid). Only one occurrence of this signature in the last 30 days. The patch (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12669" title="FLR-EC: recover data from parity code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12669"&gt;LU-12669&lt;/a&gt;, change 69392) touches only lustre/include/cl_object.h, lustre/llite/file.c, lustre/lov/lov_io.c, lustre/obdclass/cl_io.c and lustre/tests/sanity-ec.sh, none of which the ladvise path uses.&lt;br/&gt;
Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69392-ps2-d0d0ea0cba44 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
